  "transcript": "The fading summon-light leaves Renna Holt and Mirelle Voss standing among the five new arrivals in Niflheim's lobby. No third survivor stands where Edren Marr had arrived with them.\n\nRenna looks from Mirelle's blood-marked sleeve to the empty patch of stone where Edren fell, then checks her bowstring once.\n\nRenna Holt: He’s dead. Your arm is bleeding, Mirelle. Before anyone goes through another gate, that needs tending.\n\nMirelle Voss: You’re right. I let that blade through and kept fighting.\n\nMirelle tears a narrow strip from the repaired cuff, presses it to her bleeding upper arm, and offers its loose end toward Renna.\n\nMirelle Voss: Hold this a breath, please. I’m not calling myself fit just because I’m standing.\n\nRenna takes the loose end of the cloth and holds it snug against Mirelle's upper arm.\n\nRenna Holt: I've got it. Standing isn't the same as fit.",
